# Keys where the type table DELIBERATELY says something other than C, one
# per line: <t1> <op> <t2> <reason>.  tests/gold_audit.py compares every
# numeric key with the system compiler and skips these; one that starts
# agreeing with cc fails the audit, so the list cannot rot.
#
# Everything else the audit finds is a gold ERROR and gets fixed in the
# gold, not listed here.  The first run found 200 of those (comparisons
# typed as long) and fixed them.
i64 & i64 the row IS the address-of operator: the walker asks (i64, &, i64) to mean unary `&x`, which yields a pointer. A representation choice in the table's vocabulary, not a claim that `long & long` is a pointer -- bitwise & on numbers goes through the other rows.
